---
import FieldGuideLayout from '../../../components/FieldGuideLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<FieldGuideLayout
  title="LZ11 / LZS wrapper"
  description="Outer LZS wrapper + inner Nintendo LZ11 stream. Used by ~70% of containers. Decoder + encoder in src/archive/lzs.py."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Field Guide', href: `${base}/field-guide/` },
    { label: 'File Formats', href: `${base}/field-guide/file-formats/` },
    { label: 'LZ11' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    A <code>.lzs</code> file is an outer 16-byte LZS wrapper followed by a
    standard Nintendo LZ11 compressed stream. Decompressing it usually
    yields a <a href={`${base}/field-guide/file-formats/reso/`}>RESO</a>
    container.
  </p>

  <h2>Outer LZS wrapper (16 bytes)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Offset</th><th>Size</th><th>Type</th><th>Field</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x00</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td><code>magic</code></td><td><code>"1.00"</code> = <code>31 2E 30 30</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x04</code></td><td>9</td><td><code>u8[9]</code></td><td><code>reserved</code></td><td>Zero-filled</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x0D</code></td><td>3</td><td><code>char[3]</code></td><td><code>tag</code></td><td><code>"sfo"</code> = <code>73 66 6F</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x10</code></td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>LZ11 payload begins</td><td>—</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>LZ11 stream header (4 bytes)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Offset</th><th>Size</th><th>Type</th><th>Field</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>+0x00</code></td><td>1</td><td><code>u8</code></td><td>magic = <code>0x11</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x01</code></td><td>3</td><td><code>u24 LE</code></td><td>decompressed_size</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Stream body</h2>
  <p>
    Repeating blocks of <code>1 flag byte</code> + up to <code>8 chunks</code>.
    The flag byte's MSB-first bits select chunk kind: <code>0</code> = literal
    byte, <code>1</code> = back-reference.
  </p>

  <h3>Literal chunk (1 byte)</h3>
  <p>Emit the byte directly to the output buffer.</p>

  <h3>Back-reference chunk</h3>
  <p>
    The first byte's top nibble (<code>n = b1 &gt;&gt; 4</code>) selects one of
    three encodings:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>top nibble n</th><th>bytes read</th><th>length</th><th>disp</th><th>length range</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>n &gt; 1</code></td>
        <td>2 (b1 b2)</td>
        <td><code>n + 1</code></td>
        <td><code>((b1 &amp; 0xF) &lt;&lt; 8) | b2</code></td>
        <td>3..16</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>n == 0</code></td>
        <td>3 (b1 b2 b3)</td>
        <td><code>(((b1 &amp; 0xF) &lt;&lt; 4) | (b2 &gt;&gt; 4)) + 0x11</code></td>
        <td><code>((b2 &amp; 0xF) &lt;&lt; 8) | b3</code></td>
        <td>17..272</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>n == 1</code></td>
        <td>4 (b1 b2 b3 b4)</td>
        <td><code>(((b1 &amp; 0xF) &lt;&lt; 12) | (b2 &lt;&lt; 4) | (b3 &gt;&gt; 4)) + 0x111</code></td>
        <td><code>((b3 &amp; 0xF) &lt;&lt; 8) | b4</code></td>
        <td>273..65808</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    After decoding, copy <code>length</code> bytes from
    <code>output[len(output) − disp − 1 .. +length]</code> into the output.
    The copy can read bytes it just wrote (RLE-like overlapping copies).
  </p>

  <h2>Decoder reference</h2>
  <pre><code>{`# src/archive/lzs.py::decompress_lz11
def decompress_lz11(payload: bytes) -> bytes:
    decompressed_size = payload[1] | (payload[2] << 8) | (payload[3] << 16)
    out = bytearray()
    i = 4
    while len(out) < decompressed_size:
        flag = payload[i]; i += 1
        for bit in range(7, -1, -1):
            if len(out) >= decompressed_size: break
            if (flag & (1 << bit)) == 0:                       # literal
                out.append(payload[i]); i += 1
            else:                                              # back-ref
                b1 = payload[i]; b2 = payload[i+1]; i += 2
                top = b1 >> 4
                if top > 1:
                    length = top + 1
                    disp   = ((b1 & 0xF) << 8) | b2
                elif top == 0:
                    b3 = payload[i]; i += 1
                    length = (((b1 & 0xF) << 4) | (b2 >> 4)) + 0x11
                    disp   = ((b2 & 0xF) << 8) | b3
                else:                                          # top == 1
                    b3 = payload[i]; b4 = payload[i+1]; i += 2
                    length = (((b1 & 0xF) << 12) | (b2 << 4) | (b3 >> 4)) + 0x111
                    disp   = ((b3 & 0xF) << 8) | b4
                copy_from = len(out) - disp - 1
                for j in range(length):
                    out.append(out[copy_from + j])
    return bytes(out)`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Encoder</h2>
  <p>
    <code>src/archive/lzs.py::compress_lz11()</code> implements a greedy
    encoder with one-byte lookahead. Limits (per spec):
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>Length range</th><th>Displacement range</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>2-byte ref</td><td>3..0x10</td><td>1..0x1000</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3-byte ref</td><td>0x11..0x110</td><td>1..0x1000</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4-byte ref</td><td>0x111..0x10110</td><td>1..0x1000</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Output is padded to a multiple of 4 bytes (standard). The encoder is
    <strong>not</strong> byte-identical to the Nintendo SDK — different valid
    LZ11 streams can decompress to the same bytes. Round-trip
    <code>decompress(compress(x)) == x</code> is the validation test
    (passes on every blob tested, 2 KB NCGRs up to 110 KB inner RESOs).
  </p>

  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p>First 32 bytes of <code>2d/buyitem.lzs</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>{`offs  bytes                                              meaning
----  -------------------------------------------------- ----------------------------------
0000  31 2E 30 30  00 00 00 00  00 00 00 00 00  73 66 6F   wrapper magic, zeros, "sfo" tag
0010  11 80 BF 01                                          LZ11: magic=0x11, size=0x01BF80
0014  FF                                                   flag byte (0b11111111 = 8 back-refs)
0015  20 00                                                back-ref #1: n=2, length=3,
                                                                       disp=((0x0<<8)|0x00)=0
                                                                       copy 3 from out[-1]
0017  ... 7 more 2-byte refs ...`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Compression ratios (sampled)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Compressed</th><th>Decompressed</th><th>Ratio</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>buyitem.lzs</code></td><td>24,064</td><td>114,560</td><td>4.76×</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>title_pack.ofs</code> inner sub-blob 3</td><td>62,464</td><td>~88,000</td><td>~1.41×</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>global.lzs</code></td><td>varies per entry</td><td>varies</td><td>~3.5×</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>src/archive/lzs.py</code> — decoder + encoder + CLI</li>
  </ul>
</FieldGuideLayout>
